NAME
       newgrp - start a shell with another primary group

SYNOPSIS
       newgrp [GROUP]

DESCRIPTION
       newgrp starts a new shell in which GROUP is your primary group, so new
       files you create belong to GROUP. You must be a member of the group
       (or know the group's password). Without GROUP, it uses your own
       primary group from /etc/passwd. Type exit to get back to the previous
       shell.

       It is also how a user picks up a group they were just added to,
       without logging out and in again.

EXAMPLES
           newgrp devs
           touch shared.txt
           ls -l shared.txt
           exit

SEE ALSO
       id(1), groups(1), usermod(8), sg(1)
